WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.330
If it's been a while since you've seen the
first two Jumanji films or if you've avoided

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.560
the sinister game until now we've got you
covered.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.679
We've gathered everything you need to know
before you see Jumanji: The Next Level, including

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.560
past events, new characters, and more.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.420
Gather up your gear, because we're heading
back into the jungle.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.000
The original Jumanji film is based on the
1981 picture book of the same name by Chris

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.300
Van Allsburg in which a pair of siblings named
Judy and Peter Shepherd come across the titular

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.060
board game in the park.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.240
In the films, the characters come upon the
game in much the same way, with all of them

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.510
happening upon it seemingly by accident — although
the films imply that the game has a degree

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.899
of sentience to it and can manipulate circumstances
so that it can be found and played.

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:43.641
After finding a board game called Jumanji
at a construction site in 1969, Alan Parrish

00:00:43.641 --> 00:00:45.859
begins playing with his friend, Sarah Whittle.

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:49.719
However, they've barely begun to play before
Alan is sucked into the game, with a message

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.880
that he must wait in the jungle until someone
rolls a five or eight.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.070
But instead of taking her turn, the terrified
Sarah flees from the house, and the game is

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:57.620
placed in the attic.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.460
Later, in 1995, orphans Judy and Peter Shepherd
move into Alan Parrish's old house with their

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.430
aunt and discover the game in the attic.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.240
They begin to play, and Peter's roll releases
Alan from the game.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.100
"Where's my mom and dad?"

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.180
"We don't know.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.240
Everyone thought you were dead."

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:21.760
Now an adult, Alan has been living in the
jungle for the past 26 years, and he uses

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.300
the skills he's acquired there to help the
children fend off the animals and natural

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.040
disasters that emerge from the game.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.720
However, since the game from 1969 was never
finished, they have to find the adult Sarah

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.120
and convince her to take her turn so that
they can complete the game and return everything

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:35.680
to normal.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.900
After taking turns that result in the game
unleashing increasingly catastrophic levels

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.420
of mayhem and destruction, Alan finally finishes
the game and says …

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.240
"Jumanji."

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.720
Everything is returned to its pre-game state,
including Alan going back to 1969, where he

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.960
grows up to marry Sarah and prevent the accident
that killed Judy and Peter's parents.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.900
While the game of Jumanji is undeniably tricky
and deliberately misleading, it is, at its

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.300
heart, still a game.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:05.620
The rules written on the board game state:
"You roll the dice to move your token, doubles

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.909
get another turn, and the first player to
reach the end wins."

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:13.230
With each turn, the game creates a new obstacle
for the players to face, making it progressively

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.680
more difficult to finish the game.

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:19.120
Through playing, the characters learn that
no one can forfeit, leave the game, or skip

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.820
a turn, and there are consequences for attempting
to cheat in order to end the game sooner.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.310
After completing their final turn, the winning
player must say the word "Jumanji" out loud

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.480
in order to end the game.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.000
Over the course of the films, however, the
board game shifts its form to become a video

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:32.480
game.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.400
So naturally, some of the rules had to change,
but the basics have stayed the same.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:41.200
Dice-specific stipulations such as the doubles
rule no longer apply, but players still have

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:45.370
to complete the game once it's started, can't
forfeit or quit, and have to say "Jumanji"

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.480
out loud in order to finish it.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.700
In both Jumanji and Jumanji: Welcome to the
Jungle, a player gets trapped inside the game

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.680
for decades due to no one being able to beat
it.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.700
In Alan Parrish's case, his problem was that
Sarah stopped playing, and therefore didn't

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.080
roll the five or eight that was needed in
order to bring him out.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.440
Even when Judy and Peter thought they were
starting a new game, they were really just

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.720
continuing Alan and Sarah's game from 26 years
earlier.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.540
Then in Welcome to the Jungle, Alex gets caught
inside the game for 21 years after his father

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.170
finds it on the beach in 1996, where it washed
up after Alan and Sarah threw it into the

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.440
river in 1969.

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:22.900
While the original version of Jumanji was
a board game, and thus required at least two

00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:27.170
players, once it shifted into a quest-based
video game version, it became possible to

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.180
play as a solo player.

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:32.719
However, while Alex technically could've completed
the game by himself, he wound up stuck when

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.980
he came up against an obstacle he couldn't
get past on his own.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.680
Like Alan, Alex required other players to
join in later to finish the game and return

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.940
them all to their pre-game state.

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:44.980
If you're unlucky enough to get caught inside
Jumanji, and there's no one around to take

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.020
the next turn or you can't complete the game
on your own, you'll simply be stuck "playing"

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:49.560
forever.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:55.240
Unlike Sarah and Alan or Judy and Peter, the
four teenagers who go on to play the game

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.840
in Welcome to the Jungle aren't friends, siblings,
or really much of anything.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.130
Spencer, Bethany, Martha, and Fridge are all
students at Brantford High School, and that's

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.440
about where their similarities end.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:09.100
Spencer and Fridge were best friends as kids,
but now their relationship consists entirely

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.960
of Spencer doing Fridge's homework for him,
and while Spencer admires Martha from afar,

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:13.940
they don't really talk.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.380
Meanwhile, Bethany is off in her own self-absorbed
world, and she doesn't seem to notice any

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:18.940
of the others.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.740
The four are sentenced to serve detention
together in the school's storage room on a

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.720
Saturday, removing staples from magazines
so they can be recycled.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.670
Rather than engage in their tedious task,
they decide to play a video game Fridge discovers

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.920
among the shelves, and soon, they find themselves
trapped inside Jumanji.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.320
After a harrowing adventure inside the game,
including a number of near-death and actual

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.320
death experiences, the four learn to lean
on and appreciate one another, and they emerge

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.920
from the game as good friends with a new outlook
on life.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.320
Bethany learns to be brave and selfless, Martha
finds confidence, Fridge learns humility,

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.820
and Spencer learns to lead and conquer his
fears.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.090
In addition, Fridge and Spencer rekindle their
friendship, and Spencer and Martha embark

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.260
on a romantic relationship.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:02.660
While the main characters of Jumanji: Welcome
to the Jungle are Spencer, Martha, Fridge,

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:06.280
and Bethany, the people we spend the most
time watching in the film aren't technically

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.470
people at all.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.080
Instead, they're video game avatars.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:13.780
Avatars are characters that exist within the
game and are controlled by outside players,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.540
and in Welcome to the Jungle, each character
spends most of the film occupying the body

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.500
of their chosen avatar.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.200
"I look like a living garden gnome!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:21.920
Where is my phone?!"

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:22.920
"Who cares?"

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:23.500
"We are in different people's bodies."

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:28.300
Each avatar has its own strengths and weaknesses,
which remain with the avatar no matter which

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.500
player is controlling it.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.380
Ruby Roundhouse — Martha's avatar — is
proficient in karate, T'ai chi, aikido, and

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.730
dance fighting, though her weakness is venom.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:40.950
Bethany's avatar is Professor Oberon and his
strengths are cartography, archaeology, and

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.220
paleontology, and his weakness is endurance.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.230
Meanwhile, Mouse — the avatar of Fridge
— boasts an impressive knowledge of zoology

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:51.500
and an equally impressive variety of weapons,
while his weaknesses are cake, speed, and

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.060
strength.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.000
Spencer's avatar is Smolder Bravestone and
his strengths are speed, throwing boomerangs,

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.260
climbing, being "fearless," and his "smoldering
intensity."

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.040
He has zero weaknesses.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:05.820
Seaplane McDonough — the avatar of Alex
— tells us that his strengths are piloting

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.950
and margaritas, and that one of his weaknesses
is mosquitoes, but he doesn't mention what

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:10.540
the others may be.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:16.020
Although the board game version of Jumanji
had several rules specific to rolling dice,

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.460
the video game version adapts the mechanics
of its gameplay to fit its new format.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:24.040
Now instead of taking turns, the players work
together to complete levels, each with its

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.280
own goals and challenges.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:29.180
The levels get increasingly more difficult
as players progress through the game, and

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.920
all build toward an ultimate end goal.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.080
Additionally, each character starts the game
with three lives, although it's possible for

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.440
one player to transfer one of their extra
lives to another player under dire circumstances.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:44.640
If a player dies, assuming they have an additional
life, they'll respawn, along with any objects

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:49.050
they were holding when they died, appearing
in the sky over the game and landing in approximately

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:49.580
the same spot.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:54.760
Jumanji also contains several NPCs or non-player
characters that interact with the characters'

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.720
avatars and either guide them on their way
or attempt to work against them.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:03.280
The main NPCs in Welcome to the Jungle are
Nigel, who serves as a guide for the characters,

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.200
and Van Pelt, who's the game's antagonist.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:10.150
Van Pelt also existed in the board game version
of Jumanji as a big game hunter determined

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.520
to keep Alan and the other players from completing
the game.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:16.900
In Welcome to the Jungle, Van Pelt is given
a more thorough backstory and a similar goal

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.950
to the player characters, but his role as
the game's resident bad guy appears to be

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:21.680
a Jumanji constant.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.110
So what exactly happens in Jumanji: Welcome
to the Jungle?

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.960
Well, after getting trapped inside Jumanji,
and after a period of initial confusion and

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.490
denial, Spencer, Martha, Fridge, and Bethany
have to work together to deliver a magical

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:39.650
jewel called the Jaguar's Eye to a giant jaguar
statue before the sinister Russell Van Pelt

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:40.460
can get his hands on it.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:45.370
Possessed by the power of the jewel, Van Pelt
is able to control Jumanji's animals, which

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:48.020
works against the players as they attempt
to complete their task.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:52.440
The group is given clues meant to inform their
quests, which leads them to Alex's avatar,

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:57.240
who'd started the game in 1996 but had gotten
stuck when he found himself down to his last

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.430
life on a challenge he didn't know how to
complete.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:03.940
Drawing on their avatars' collective strengths,
the group is finally able to beat the level

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:07.800
that had thwarted Alex for so long, although
Alex loses his last life in the process, and

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.900
Bethany has to transfer one of her extra lives
to him through CPR.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.170
The five players reach the statue, return
the jewel, and call out, "Jumanji," ending

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:15.740
the game.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.680
Shaking hands with each of them, Nigel returns
them to their lives at the moment before they

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.340
entered the game.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.340
The four Brantford High teens walk to the
previously run-down Vreeke home, where they

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:29.180
encounter a now grown-up Alex, who tells them
he'd emerged from the game in 1996 and had

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.600
lived a good life, naming his oldest daughter
Bethany.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.980
Later, the four teens destroy the game.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:39.280
Almost every major player from Jumanji: Welcome
to the Jungle is coming back for Jumanji:

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:42.380
The Next Level, although we'll get to see
several of them in a brand new light.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.360
In fact, the entire main cast including Rhys
Darby's Nigel and Colin Hanks' Alex will be

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.480
returning for the next installment in the
series.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:53.500
The only significant character from Welcome
to the Jungle who hasn't been confirmed for

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:56.840
the sequel is Bobby Cannavale, who played
the villainous Van Pelt.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:01.260
However, while most of the faces in The Next
Level will be familiar, some of the actors

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.860
will be portraying totally different characters.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.720
Due to Jumanji's use of avatars, only Karen
Gillan will be portraying the same player

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:08.980
as she did in Welcome to the Jungle.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.800
Fridge, who played as Kevin Hart's Mouse Finbar
the first time around, will now be controlling

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.499
Jack Black's Shelly Oberon, while Dwayne "The
Rock" Johnson and Hart will be portraying

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:22.020
the avatars of two brand-new characters: Spencer's
grandfather, Eddie, and Eddie's friend, Milo.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.009
We've yet to learn which avatars Bethany and
Spencer wind up controlling, or if Alex re-enters

00:09:27.009 --> 00:09:30.600
the game at all, but one thing's for sure
this game will be very different from the

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.160
last one.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.670
"We're gonna die."

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.670
"We did die."

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.360
"Are we in hell?"

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:34.920
"I knew it."

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.720
Joining the cast for Jumanji: The Next Level
are comedic acting legends Danny DeVito and

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:44.260
Danny Glover, playing Spencer's grandfather,
Eddie Gilpin, and his friend, Milo Walker,

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:44.820
respectively.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.500
If The Next Level follows the same format
as Welcome to the Jungle, we don't expect

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.700
to see DeVito and Glover on screen for very
long, but it looks like the characters will

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.550
still have a significant presence in the movie
after they accidentally enter the game and

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:00.600
wind up controlling the avatars portrayed
by Dwayne Johnson and Kevin Hart.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.920
Also coming aboard for the next Jumanji outing
are Once Upon a Time's Dania Ramirez and Crazy

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.560
Rich Asians and The Farewell star Awkwafina,
both in undisclosed roles.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.560
While Ramirez doesn't appear in the trailer
at all, the brief glimpse we get of Awkwafina

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.440
suggests that she'll be playing a character
within the game, although whether she'll be

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:19.889
another avatar or a new NPC is anyone's guess.

00:10:19.889 --> 00:10:24.329
Whoever she is, sources have told The Hollywood
Reporter that Awkwafina's role is more significant

00:10:24.329 --> 00:10:28.730
than just a cameo leading us to guess that
she's likely either an avatar for one of the

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:32.980
players possibly Spencer, Bethany, or even
Alex or she's the game's new villain.

